{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, scvi_n200, ViT-L, singleprofile, concat) achieved 0.532 acc, while config_005 (image_only, ViT-L, singleprofile) achieved only 0.227 acc. This large gap suggests RNA carries most of the signal, but we cannot yet quantify how much of the multimodal performance comes from RNA alone versus the image modality. Question: config_008 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates the RNA contribution by removing the image modality while keeping the same RNA encoder and profile setting as config_002. If RNA-only ≈ 0.53, the image adds little and future effort should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation choices; if RNA-only is substantially lower, the image modality is genuinely complementary and fusion strategy becomes a high-value design axis. Why this is the best next experiment: it is the single most informative ablation given only two completed runs—it resolves the fundamental uncertainty about modality contribution with a minimal, controlled change (only model_setting differs from config_002), and its result will most efficiently direct all subsequent experiments under the limited budget."
}

